            "@id": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/08/21/2026-17183/regulation-crypto-assets"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-08-21",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1645,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1644
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1646",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationByNetworkLineItems",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/securities-and-exchange-commission",
          "dct:title": "Regulation Crypto Assets (proposed), Release Nos. 33-11434; 34-106150, File No. S7-2026-27, 91 FR 54510 (Aug. 21, 2026)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "17 CFR 228.100 (related person); 91 FR 54607",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"founders, promoters, employees, affiliates, and any person that is a director, officer, trustee, consultant, contractor, or advisor to the issuer, in each case together with any immediate family members\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/08/21/2026-17183/regulation-crypto-assets"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-08-21",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1646,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1645
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1647",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationByNetworkLineItems",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/securities-and-exchange-commission",
          "dct:title": "17 CFR 230.405 (Securities Act Rule 405), incorporated by 17 CFR 228.100",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "17 CFR 230.405 (affiliate)",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"An affiliate of, or person affiliated with, a specified person, is a person that directly, or indirectly through one or more intermediaries, controls or is controlled by, or is under common control with, the person specified.\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/chapter-II/part-230/subject-group-ECFR6e651a4c86c0174/section-230.405"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-09-01",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1647,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1646
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1648",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationByNetworkLineItems",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/securities-and-exchange-commission",
          "dct:title": "17 CFR 230.405 (Securities Act Rule 405), incorporated by 17 CFR 228.100",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "17 CFR 230.405 (control)",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"the possession, direct or indirect, of the power to direct or cause the direction of the management and policies of a person, whether through the ownership of voting securities, by contract, or otherwise\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/chapter-II/part-230/subject-group-ECFR6e651a4c86c0174/section-230.405"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-09-01",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1648,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1647
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1649",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationByNetworkLineItems",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/rutgers-carlab-engineering-sciences-laboratory-ibn-tofail-university-auditchain-labs-ag",
          "dct:title": "El Imami, Oh, Meyers, Brennan, Vasarhelyi, Sannella, Egan et al., Beyond the Fiat Vault: Evaluating Machine-Readable Blockchain Disclosures for Systemic Safety, Operational Security, and MEV Conflict Mitigation (BNP Disclosure Taxonomy paper)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "PDF p. 11",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"Extends network participation mapping to affiliate perimeter: affiliate identification and participation details, services provided, and conflicts of interest analysis.\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://raw.rutgers.edu/bnp-disclosure-taxonomy.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-09-27",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1649,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1648
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1650",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationByNetworkLineItems",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/rutgers-carlab-engineering-sciences-laboratory-ibn-tofail-university-auditchain-labs-ag",
          "dct:title": "El Imami, Oh, Meyers, Brennan, Vasarhelyi, Sannella, Egan et al., Beyond the Fiat Vault: Evaluating Machine-Readable Blockchain Disclosures for Systemic Safety, Operational Security, and MEV Conflict Mitigation (BNP Disclosure Taxonomy paper)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "PDF p. 12",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"Replicates the entire affiliate disclosure schema per individual affiliate entity using the AffiliateIdentifierTypedAxis.\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://raw.rutgers.edu/bnp-disclosure-taxonomy.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-09-27",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1650,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1649
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1651",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationByNetworkLineItems",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/auditchain-labs-ag",
          "dct:title": "Comment letter to the FDIC on GENIUS Act requirements and standards, RIN 3064-AG19, 91 FR 18534 (May 14, 2026)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "PDF p. 4",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"the affiliate has the ability to influence transaction ordering, censor transfers, extract MEV\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://www.fdic.gov/federal-register-publications/auditchain-labs-ag-jason-meyers-rin-3064-ag19.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-05-14",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1651,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1650
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1652",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationByNetworkLineItems",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/rutgers-carlab-engineering-sciences-laboratory-ibn-tofail-university-auditchain-labs-ag",
          "dct:title": "El Imami, Oh, Meyers, Brennan, Vasarhelyi, Sannella, Egan and Ouatik El Alaoui, Testing Machine-Readable Compliance: Validation Gaps and Omission Invariance in Stablecoin Reporting",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "PDF p. 16",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"Perimeter attestation improves accountability by turning silent omission into an affirmative representation, but computational detection requires an independently maintained reference point.\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://raw.rutgers.edu/Testing-Machine-Readable-Compliance.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-09-27",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1652,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1651
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1653",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationByNetworkLineItems",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/rutgers-carlab-engineering-sciences-laboratory-ibn-tofail-university-auditchain-labs-ag",
          "dct:title": "El Imami, Oh, Meyers, Brennan, Vasarhelyi, Sannella, Egan and Ouatik El Alaoui, Testing Machine-Readable Compliance: Validation Gaps and Omission Invariance in Stablecoin Reporting",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "PDF p. 1",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"when all completeness-relevant operands originate within the filing, a consistently omitted affiliate can leave internal validation satisfied\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://raw.rutgers.edu/Testing-Machine-Readable-Compliance.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-09-27",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1653,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1652
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1654",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationByNetworkLineItems",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/supreme-court-of-the-united-states",
          "dct:title": "TSC Industries, Inc. v. Northway, Inc., 426 U.S. 438 (1976)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "426 U.S. at 449",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"there must be a substantial likelihood that the disclosure of the omitted fact would have been viewed by the reasonable investor as having significantly altered the \"total mix\" of information made available.\" Relied on for BNP disclosure in Auditchain's FDIC comments (RIN 3064-AG19, May 14, 2026; RIN 3064-AG20 supplemental, Mar. 9, 2026).",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ll/usrep/usrep426/usrep426438/usrep426438.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "1976-06-14",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1654,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1653
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1655",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationByNetworkLineItems",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/financial-accounting-standards-board",
          "dct:title": "FASB Accounting Standards Codification, Topic 850, Related Party Disclosures",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "Topic 850",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Topic title as published: \"Topic 850, Related Party Disclosures\" (FASB ASU 2023-06)",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://storage.fasb.org/ASU%202023-06.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2023-10-09",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1655,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1654
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1656",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AggregatedNetworkConcentrationTable",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/securities-and-exchange-commission",
          "dct:title": "Regulation Crypto Assets (proposed), Release Nos. 33-11434; 34-106150, File No. S7-2026-27, 91 FR 54510 (Aug. 21, 2026)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "17 CFR 228.103(b)(10); 91 FR 54608",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"This description must avoid generalized statements and include only factors specific to the covered investment contract, the issuer, the subject crypto asset, and the associated crypto network or associated crypto application\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/08/21/2026-17183/regulation-crypto-assets"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-08-21",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1656,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1655
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1657",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AggregatedNetworkConcentrationTable",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/securities-and-exchange-commission",
          "dct:title": "Regulation Crypto Assets (proposed), Release Nos. 33-11434; 34-106150, File No. S7-2026-27, 91 FR 54510 (Aug. 21, 2026)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "17 CFR 228.103(b)(9); 91 FR 54608",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"including information regarding the technology infrastructure, types of participants, and other parties and systems using the subject crypto asset and the associated crypto network or associated crypto application\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/08/21/2026-17183/regulation-crypto-assets"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-08-21",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1657,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1656
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1658",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AggregatedNetworkConcentrationTable",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/rutgers-carlab-engineering-sciences-laboratory-ibn-tofail-university-auditchain-labs-ag",
          "dct:title": "El Imami, Oh, Meyers, Brennan, Vasarhelyi, Sannella, Egan et al., Beyond the Fiat Vault: Evaluating Machine-Readable Blockchain Disclosures for Systemic Safety, Operational Security, and MEV Conflict Mitigation (BNP Disclosure Taxonomy paper)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "PDF p. 12",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"Computes combined issuer and affiliate network control as a single consolidated control metric to see if it could influence consensus outcomes.\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://raw.rutgers.edu/bnp-disclosure-taxonomy.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-09-27",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1658,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1657
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1659",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AggregatedNetworkConcentrationTable",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/auditchain-labs-ag",
          "dct:title": "Comment to the FDIC on proposed Forms PS-01, PS-01a and PS-02, OMB No. 3064-0225 (Sept. 23, 2026)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "PDF p. 9",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"Whoever operates the validators, miners and staking infrastructure of the networks … decides which transactions are ordered, included, delayed or excluded.\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://www.fdic.gov/federal-register-publications/auditchain-jason-meyers-omb-3064-0225.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-09-23",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1659,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1658
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1660",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AggregatedNetworkConcentrationTable",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/auditchain-labs-ag",
          "dct:title": "Comment letter to the FDIC on GENIUS Act requirements and standards, RIN 3064-AG19, 91 FR 18534 (May 14, 2026)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "PDF p. 3",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"Validator concentration ratios, affiliate consensus participation, MEV mitigation policies, and slashing event histories each bear directly on the risk\"",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://www.fdic.gov/federal-register-publications/auditchain-labs-ag-jason-meyers-rin-3064-ag19.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "2026-05-14",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1660,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1659
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1661",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AggregatedNetworkConcentrationTable",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/supreme-court-of-the-united-states",
          "dct:title": "TSC Industries, Inc. v. Northway, Inc., 426 U.S. 438 (1976)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "426 U.S. at 449",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"An omitted fact is material if there is a substantial likelihood that a reasonable shareholder would consider it important in deciding how to vote.\" Relied on for BNP disclosure in Auditchain's FDIC comments (RIN 3064-AG19, May 14, 2026; RIN 3064-AG20 supplemental, Mar. 9, 2026).",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ll/usrep/usrep426/usrep426438/usrep426438.pdf"
          },
          "dct:date": {
            "@value": "1976-06-14",
            "@type": "xsd:date"
          },
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 1661,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 1660
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:reference/1662",
          "@type": "cmns-doc:Reference",
          "xbrlb:referenceOf": "regca:AggregatedNetworkConcentrationTable",
          "dct:type": "xbrl-role:commentaryRef",
          "dct:publisher": "regca-complete:publisher/federal-deposit-insurance-corporation",
          "dct:title": "GENIUS Act Requirements and Standards for FDIC-Supervised Permitted Payment Stablecoin Issuers and Insured Depository Institutions (proposed rule), 91 FR 18534 (Apr. 10, 2026)",
          "dct:bibliographicCitation": "91 FR 18548 (proposed 12 CFR 350.6(b))",
          "cmns-docc:hasTextualContent": "Verbatim: \"including reliance on distributed ledger(s) or distributed ledger protocol(s) to process and record payment stablecoin transactions\" Proposed banking-agency standard for payment stablecoin issuers, cited by analogy; addressed in Auditchain's FDIC comment (RIN 3064-AG19, May 14, 2026).",
          "cmns-doc:refersTo": {
            "@id": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/04/10/2026-06974/genius-act-requirements-and-standards-for-fdic-supervised-permitted-payment-stablecoin-issuers-and"
