            "@type": "xsd:anyURI"
          },
          "cmns-dsg:hasDescription": "True if, during the two most recent fiscal years and any later interim period before the resignation, declination or dismissal, there was any disagreement with the former accountant on accounting principles or practices, financial statement disclosure, or auditing scope or procedure that, if not resolved to its satisfaction, would have caused it to refer to the matter in its report. Includes disagreements later resolved; a difference of opinion is enough, and an oral communication from the engagement partner generally suffices (Item 304(a)(1)(iv); Instructions 4-5).",
