        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:mvf/entry/IssuerBlockchainNetworkParticipationForPeriodAbstract",
          "@type": "mvf:MVFEntry",
          "cmns-col:isIncludedIn": "regca-complete:mvf/dictionary",
          "mvf:hasDescriptiveReference": {
            "@value": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Auditchain/sec-reg-ca-taxonomy/main/SBRM/report.xsd#regca_IssuerBlockchainNetworkParticipationForPeriodAbstract",
            "@type": "xsd:anyURI"
          },
          "cmns-dsg:hasDescription": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. The items of the issuer's network participation that are reported for a period: the financial figures (revenue, share of total revenue, expenses, net income, capital expenditures) for the period of the financial statements, validator uptime and governance votes over the period, and the descriptions. The items reported as of a date (protocol, network type, nodes and validators, stake and hash-power share, governance tokens, the dependency indicators) are in \"Rule 103(b)(9) — issuer blockchain network participation\". Both tables use the same network identifier, so a network has the same number in both. Element names, datatypes and period types are unchanged from the BNP taxonomy filed with the FDIC; only the grouping into two tables, one of items reported as of a date and one of items reported for a period, is new, so that each table has one date column.",
          "mvf:hasSemanticReference": [
            "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/08/21/2026-17183/regulation-crypto-assets",
            "https://raw.rutgers.edu/bnp-disclosure-taxonomy.pdf",
            "https://www.fdic.gov/federal-register-publications/supplemental-comment-auditchain-labs-ag-jason-meyers-rin-3064-ag20",
            "https://raw.rutgers.edu/Testing-Machine-Readable-Compliance.pdf",
            "https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/ll/usrep/usrep426/usrep426438/usrep426438.pdf",
            "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/04/10/2026-06974/genius-act-requirements-and-standards-for-fdic-supervised-permitted-payment-stablecoin-issuers-and",
            "https://www.fdic.gov/federal-register-publications/auditchain-labs-ag-jason-meyers-rin-3064-ag19.pdf"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:mvf/term/standard-label/IssuerBlockchainNetworkParticipationForPeriodAbstract",
