          "cmns-col:isIncludedIn": "regca-complete:mvf/vocabulary/xbrl-taxonomy",
          "cmns-dsg:isDefinedIn": "regca-complete:mvf/vocabulary/xbrl-taxonomy"
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-complete:mvf/entry/ThirdPartyServiceProviderArrangementsForPeriodAbstract",
          "@type": "mvf:MVFEntry",
          "cmns-col:isIncludedIn": "regca-complete:mvf/dictionary",
          "mvf:hasDescriptiveReference": {
            "@value": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Auditchain/sec-reg-ca-taxonomy/main/SBRM/report.xsd#regca_ThirdPartyServiceProviderArrangementsForPeriodAbstract",
            "@type": "xsd:anyURI"
          },
          "cmns-dsg:hasDescription": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. The items of the third-party service provider arrangements that are reported for a period: for each provider, the services it provides, the fees paid to it, and its conflicts of interest and their mitigation. The items reported as of a date (whether it provides blockchain network services, its name and legal entity identifier, whether it has conflicts of interest) are in \"Rule 103(b)(9) — third-party service provider arrangements\". Both tables use the same provider identifier. Element names, datatypes and period types are unchanged from Section 8 of the BNP questionnaire; only the grouping into two tables, one of items reported as of a date and one of items reported for a period, is new, so that each table has one date column.",
